Z||000000||Formula||06-14-2000||06:08 PM||||How far is my sppedo off when I use 225/60-15s on the back and 205/60-15s front tires?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-14-2000||08:01 PM||||I don't know the calculations (math was never my strong subject), but I wouldn't imagine it would be off by much.  The front tire size doesn't matter (I don't think) and I think it originally wore 215s on the rear so you aren't off by much.  I know this doesn't help much but maybe it'll ease your mind until one of the brains comes up with the answer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-15-2000||02:48 AM||||Your speedo would read 3.8% slower. Only the back tires matter because that's where the speedo is read from.<BR>Here is a site for tire/speedo calculations<P><BR> <A HREF="http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||06-15-2000||09:42 AM||||Why do want to change it??? It's a good excuse to go a few miles over the limit.  I'm just kiddin'.  Anyway, Oreif is correct. This means if the speedometer read 60 MPH, you'd actually be going 62 or 63.  If your speedometer read 100 MPH (hypothetical  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) you'd actually be going 103 or 104.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||06-15-2000||10:09 AM||||Wow..According to the calc. my speedo is approx. 10% off..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> (i have 215/70/14's all the way around)||||reg||1
